должен всегда проходить, а у неё — fail если result непуст).\n**Третье:** #include <string_view>.\n**Мелочь:** переменная both_empty вводит в заблуждение; сообщение.\n\nThen propose final structure:\n```cpp\nif (argc != 4) { usage; return 1; }\nstd::string_view flag{argv[1]};\nif (flag != \"--contains\" && flag != \"--equal\") { unknown; return 1; }\n\nread both files...\n\nif (flag == \"--equal\") {\n    rm_crlf_symbols(result);\n    rm_crlf_symbols(expected);\n    if (result != expected) { msg; return 1; }\n    return 0;\n}\n// contains\nreturn (result.find(expected) != std::string::npos) ? 0 : 1;\n```\n\nWait — but for contains with empty expected: find returns 0 → not npos → return 0. Good. For equal with both empty → == → 0. Good. So no special empty handling needed at all.\n\nThis is clean. I'll present it as the recommended structure, ask if she agrees.\n\nNote the user's is_empty wrapper was an attempt to preserve the original empty special-case. I should explain WHY it's now unnecessary (both modes handle empty naturally), which addresses the concern behind it.\n\nLet me write concisely. In plan mode, no edits.",
